What is JDK, JRE, JVM

JDK:Java development Kit->is a complete software development kit used to develop java application   , it contains JRE,Java complier etc.
JVM: Java virtual machine->it provide environment required for java program to run
JRE:Java Runtime Enviornment-->it execute bytecode.


What is bytecode
Bytecode is an intermidite code generated by java complier,after compilling a .java file and stored in a class

JVM reads and execute this bytecode.

What does “write once, run anywhere” mean (1–2 short paragraphs)
it because java is platform independent bytecode,which is then executed by JVM,each platform has there JVM implementation that converts bytecode into native machine instructor.